# script-src hashes whitelist the page's remaining inline <script> snippets:
#   1) Organization JSON-LD (every page, sitewide in Base.astro)
#   2) Astro's IntersectionObserver loader (client:visible bootstrap)
#   3) Astro's astro-island custom-element registration
#   4) homepage JSON-LD @graph — WebSite + SoftwareApplication + FAQPage
#      (homepage only, in index.astro). The FAQ accordion is JS-free (native
#      <details>), so it adds no script hash.
#   5) /digital-waste-tracking JSON-LD @graph — Article + FAQPage +
#      BreadcrumbList (that page only). The DWTS timeline on it is driven by
#      an external module, so the page adds this one hash and no more.
#   6) /walkthrough JSON-LD @graph — VideoObject + BreadcrumbList. NOTE: the
#      VideoObject's thumbnailUrl is the build-hashed /_astro path of the poster
#      image, so REPLACING src/assets/walkthrough-poster.jpg changes this hash
#      even though no markup moved. Same class of trap as dwtsFaqItems below.
#   7) /install JSON-LD @graph — BreadcrumbList only.
#   8) /security JSON-LD @graph — BreadcrumbList only. The contents rail's
#      scroll-spy is an external module (src/scripts/security.ts) and the PDF
#      download is a plain <a download>, so the page adds this one hash and no
#      more.
# The player facade (src/scripts/walkthrough.ts) and the install-guide platform
# detector (src/scripts/install.ts) both import src/scripts/lib/env.ts, so they
# are emitted as external /_astro/*.js like the rest — neither adds a hash.
# The mobile-menu handler and the cinematic bundle are NO LONGER inline: they
# import a shared module (src/scripts/lib/env.ts), so Astro emits them as
# external /_astro/*.js files covered by script-src 'self'. Deliberate —
# inline-script hashes silently drift when the build minifier changes (this
# broke prod once, 13 Jul 2026); external 'self' scripts don't. Don't reinline.
# The 8 hashes below are stable (JSON-LD is plain JSON; Astro's runtime scripts
# don't re-minify per build). Regenerate only after an Astro version bump OR
# after editing:
#   - src/layouts/Base.astro (the Organization JSON-LD)
#   - src/pages/index.astro (the homepage JSON-LD @graph)
#   - src/pages/digital-waste-tracking.astro (its JSON-LD @graph) — note this
#     one is built from src/config/dwts.ts, so editing the FAQ or the
#     milestones in that config ALSO changes this hash.
#   - src/pages/walkthrough.astro, src/pages/install.astro or
#     src/pages/security.astro (their @graphs)
#
# media-src is the ONE cross-origin allowance on this site, and it exists for a
# single file: the walkthrough MP4 in Supabase Storage, played by a native
# <video> on /walkthrough. Three things keep it honest and all three must stay
# true —
#   1) It is CLICK-TO-LOAD. No <video> element exists until the visitor presses
#      play (src/scripts/walkthrough.ts). That affirmative action is what makes
#      it lawful under PECR without a consent banner — Supabase's CDN sets a
#      __cf_bm cookie on supabase.co when the file is fetched. Preloading,
#      prefetching or hover-triggering would break that and make /cookies wrong.
#   2) media-src ONLY, and NO script-src entry — this is a direct file played by
#      a native element, not an embedded player, so no third-party JavaScript
#      ever runs on the page. If anyone swaps this for an embed SDK, the whole
#      privacy argument in /cookies §4 has to be rewritten first.
#   3) The origin is pinned exactly, and mirrors VIDEO_URL in
#      src/config/walkthrough.ts — change one and you must change the other or
#      playback silently dies. Any other media host is blocked outright: that is
#      intended, not a bug. Disclose in /cookies before you widen it.
# There is no frame-src entry: nothing on this site is framed. It falls back to
# default-src 'self'. (An earlier plan used a Cloudflare Stream iframe and
# needed one; the direct-file approach replaced it and is strictly less
# invasive — a media request instead of a third-party player.)
